What is Managed Identity?

Managed Identity is an Azure-managed identity assigned to an Azure resource.

Azure creates and manages the credentials automatically.

No secrets or passwords are required.

Example

Without Managed Identity:

VM
 │
 ▼
Username
Password

Secrets must be stored and rotated.

With Managed Identity:

VM
 │
 ▼
Managed Identity
 │
 ▼
Azure Key Vault

Azure handles authentication automatically.

Types of Managed Identity
1. System-Assigned

Created automatically for one Azure resource.

VM
 │
 ▼
Managed Identity

If the VM is deleted, the identity is deleted too.

2. User-Assigned

Created independently.

Managed Identity
     │
 ┌───┴────┐
 ▼        ▼
VM1      VM2

Can be shared by multiple Azure resources.

Service Principal vs Managed Identity
Service Principal	Managed Identity
Used by external apps	Used by Azure resources
You manage secrets/certificates (unless using workload identity/OIDC)	Azure manages credentials
Works outside Azure	Azure resources only
Common with GitHub Actions, Jenkins	Common with VMs, AKS, App Service
