Key Takeaways
Microsoft Entra ID manages identities.
Authentication verifies identity; Authorization grants permissions.
RBAC defines who can do what and where.
Service Principals are identities for applications and automation.
Managed Identities provide secure, passwordless authentication for Azure resources.
Azure DevOps Update

One important note based on current best practices:

In modern Azure DevOps and GitHub Actions pipelines, OpenID Connect (OIDC) / Workload Identity Federation is increasingly replacing client-secret-based Service Principals. It allows GitHub Actions to authenticate to Azure without storing secrets. We'll cover this in detail during the GitHub Actions and Azure authentication modules, since it's the recommended production approach today.